      <hr />

      <div id="DUC-Cloud-CRM" style="padding-left:10%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:xx-large; font-weight:bold"> DUC Cloud CRM </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify;">
            The DUC Cloud CRM (Customer Relationship Management) is an online application that lets the sales team view relevant information pertaining to prospective  and current clients anywhere, anytime and on any computing platform. <br />  <br />
            All the user would need to access this customer information is an active account in the DUC ERP system, an internet connection, any computer that can connect to the Internet, and an internet browser.  <br />  <br />
            Please note that the software design, processes and information contained within the DUC Cloud CRM and its offline variant, the DUC CRM, is confidential to the company and is not meant to be shared with other organizations especially those that have conflicting and competing interests with our company.  <br />  <br />
            The Cloud CRM is composed of tabs that categorize the entire client list into stages in the sales pipeline.  Another important tab aside from these customer grouping tabs is the sales dashboard.  These tabs are described in greater detail below:
            </div> <br />
      </div>

      <hr />

      <div id="Major-Functional-Tabs" style="padding-left:10%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:xx-large; font-weight:bold"> Major Functional Tabs </div> <br />                        
      </div>

      <div id="My-Dashboard" style="padding-left:15%; padding-right:10%"> 
        <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> My Dashboard </div> <br /> 
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify">
            This tab presents a real-time snapshot of your sales team's objectives and actual performance.  The following contents are found in this tab:
            </div> <br />
      </div>            

      <div id="The-Sales-to-Quota-Graph" style="padding-left:20%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> The Sales to Quota Graph </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify"">
            This graph shows the user a comparison between the group's sales targets versus the actual sales performance.  This graph visually tells the user whether or not the sales performance is below, at or above the expected goals.  Sales are based on invoiced items and not on sales orders.  <br /> <br />
            Sales goals are set per month and may be ladderized.  This means that the sales goals may be set in a way that there is an easy target, a medium target and a hard target.  Compensation is set to match the difficulty of these sales targets.  The harder the target, the higher the reward. <br /> <br />
            Graphs for actual sales performance and the ladderized sales goals are presented side by side and grouped per month.  Both currency and percentage values are presented for quicker and more high-impact visualization of goals and performance.  The last 6 months of sales performance and targets are presented in this graph. 
            </div> <br />
      </div>
      
      <div id="The-Comparative-Sales-Graph" style="padding-left:20%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> The Comparative Sales Graph </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify"">
            This graph shows the full-year historical sales performance of your sales team.  The graph runs from left to right, with January on the left-most side and December on the right-most side.  This graph also shows the historical sales performance of the previous year so that a meaningful comparison can be made on a month-on-month basis.
            </div> <br />
      </div>

      <div id="Special-Incentive-Items" style="padding-left:20%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> Special Incentive Items </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify"">
            This table shows you the list of items that have add-on incentives to your regular incentives.  This tells you what items they are, how much additional incentives they carry, what minimum volume you need to sell to qualify for the add-on incentives, and your achieved sales for these items.
            </div> <br />
      </div>

      <div id="Targets-and-Earned-Incentives" style="padding-left:20%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> Targets and Earned Incentives </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify"">
            The targets table shows you your sales targets as well as collection targets.  This section also shows you your earned incentives based on these targets.  The Cloud CRM and its accompanying backend systems are capable of computing your sales team's incentives automatically to provide you with an efficient and effective means of viewing your performance, your incentives and online forms for you to actually get compensated. <br /> <br />
            Your sales commissions are based on four factors: <br />
            1. Actual Sales versus Sales Targets <br />
            2. Actual Collections Days Overdue versus Collection Days Overdue Targets <br />
            3. Special Incentive Items, subject to Collection Age Targets <br />
            4. Allocation plan of Incentives for the individual members of your sales team <br /> <br />
            Your incentive rate is based on the 1st factor listed above.   This factor only qualifies your actual sales invoices for the commission.  For example, let's suppose your sales team's target for the month of January is P300,000 and a 0.65% commission is to be given out if this target is achieved.  Your team achieves the P300,000 goal.  This means that all of the sales invoices made for that month of January will be tagged by the system as "Qualified for Incentive".   At this stage, the sales incentive is not yet to be paid out. <br /> <br />
            Payout is based on actual collection performance, the 2nd factor listed above.  The company pays your team only when you are able to fully collect a sales invoice that is tagged as being qualified for incentive. <br /> <br />
            Please note that invoices that are not fully paid are still "open" invoices and the age of collection for "open" invoices grows older each passing day.  "Open" invoices are not included in the computation of incentive payout.  This rule is applicable for regular incentives and special incentive items.  There is no exception to this rule.  As the days of overdue grows older, the lesser sales incentives you will be able to get.  A pie graph is shown to you for visualization of potential incentive losses due to poor collection performance. <br /> <br />
            Special incentive items are add-on opportunities for you to increase overall incentives.  These special incentives are also subject to collection rules.  Please see section below on Special Incentive Items for more information. <br /> <br />
            Finally, the CRM and its backend systems are capable of determining your payout distribution plan among your team members.  Field sales people (Outside Sales Force) usually get a higher compensation compared to sales desk officers (Inside Sales Force).  However, sales desk officers are eligible to join multiple teams (and thus increase income opportunities), while fields sales officers are not.
            </div> <br />
      </div>      

      <div id="Sales-Pipeline" style="padding-left:20%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> Sales Pipeline </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify"">
            The Sales Pipeline is a table that shows you, in brief summary, how many clients you have on the leads, prospects and closed deal stages sorted according to sales potential, estimated close dates and rating (Please see section below on rating for more information).
            </div> <br />
      </div>

     <div id="My-Leads" style="padding-left:15%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> My Leads </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify;">
            The "My Leads" tab shows you a list of previous clients that have not made any transaction with our company for more than two months counting back from today.  These clients need to be reactivated for economic relationships to continue. <br /> <br />
            When you rate a client as "Cold" in any of the "My Leads" or "My Qualified Prospects" tab, that client with the cold rating is automatically sent to the "My Leads" tab.  Clients listed on the "My Closed Deals" tab will be transferred to the "My Leads" tab (in case of a Cold Rating) only after 15 days from their last invoice date. <br /> <br />
            The clients listed on this tab will usually take more time and effort to reactivate than clients who are further along the sales pipeline.  It is wise to work your "My Qualified Prospects" tab first before this one.  However, having a good and steady stream of leads is essential to grow your sales.  <br /> <br />
            Therefore, good time management and client prioritization is important to your success. 
            </div> <br />
      </div>

      <div id="My-Qualified-Prospects" style="padding-left:15%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> My Qualified Prospects </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify;">
            The "My Qualified Prospects" tab shows you a list of previous clients that have not made any transaction with our company within at least the last 8 days up to 2 months.  The relationship with these clients are still warm and it usually does not take a lot to close future deals with clients on this list.  In short, there are higher chances of closing deals with clients listed on this tab compared to those in the "My Leads" tab.  <br /> <br />
            Care must be given to increase the client list on this tab and not to lose them to the competition.  You are strongly advised to check the "My Prospects Tab" everyday to protect your market from being taken by competitors. <br /> <br />
            When you rate a client as "Warm" or "Hot" in any of the "My Leads" or "My Qualified Prospects" tab, that client with the "Warm" or "Hot" rating is automatically sent to the "My Qualified Prospects" tab.  Clients listed on the "My Closed Deals" tab will be transferred to the "My Qualified Prospects" tab (in case of a Warm or Hot Rating) only after 15 days from their last invoice date. <br /> <br />
            The next logical step for you is to facilitate a sale to these clients so that they can be moved to the "My Closed Deals" tab.
            </div> <br />
      </div>

      <div id="My-Closed-Deals" style="padding-left:15%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> My Closed Deals </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify;">
            The "My Closed Deals" tab shows you a list of previous clients that have made a purchase from our company within the last 15 days.  You are advised to pay them a courtesy call over the phone or in person to check up on them and thank them for their business. <br /> <br />
            15 days after the client's latest invoice date, the client record is automatically moved from the "My Closed Deals" to the "My Qualified Prospects" tab if the rating for the client is either "Warm" or "Hot".  <br /> <br />
            If you change the rating for the client in the "My Closed Deal" tab to a "Cold" rating, then that client is moved to the "My Leads" tab after 15 days of the client's latest invoice date.  <br /> <br />
            By default, all clients in the "My Closed Deals" are assigned a "Warm" rating by the Cloud CRM.  You can change this rating at anytime.
            </div> <br />
      </div>

      <hr />
      
      <div id="Functionalities-Inside-the-Tabs" style="padding-left:10%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:xx-large; font-weight:bold"> Functionalities Inside the Tabs </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify;">
            A search box is found at the top right  section of each tab.  You may enter keywords that pertain to the client name or address and the Cloud CRM will find the record of your client in its database.  <br /> <br />
            An example of a useful application for the search box is to search for certain locations/ streets such as "Bajada".  The resulting list will show all of your clients that have the word "Bajada" in their address or company name.  This is very useful especially if you are on field doing client calls.  This functionality can increase your efficiency and effectiveness on the field.<br /> <br />
            Please note that the search is limited to your client list and will not show you the clients of other teams.  This is done on purpose to prevent "sniping" of clients from our other teams.<br /> <br />
            In addition to the search box, each tab contains data columns such as:<br />
            1. Days Since Last Purchase<br />
            2. Company Name<br />
            3. Address<br />
            4. Estimated Value/Month<br />
            5. Estimated Close Date<br />
            6. Rating<br /> <br />
            Clicking (via mouse) or touching (on a tablet/pad) a column header will sort the entire client list on the tab according to the column header that was clicked or touched.  You might be interested in sorting the clients on the "My Qualified Prospects" according to "Estimated Value" so that you can pursue clients with the highest value first.  You simply have to click or touch the column header to sort the list according to what's important to you.
            </div> <br />
      </div>

      <div id="Company-Name" style="padding-left:15%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> Company Name </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify;">
            Clicking or touching a specific company name such as "ABC Company" on the list will result in a new browser tab being opened.  This new browser tab will contain important customer information such as contact details, purchase history, rating, estimated value, estimated close date, "Cloud Notes" and more.  The opening of a new browser tab is designed on purpose to save you  a lot of time and effort by avoiding unnecessary loading and reloading of web pages. <br /> <br />
            It is advised that you review the customer profile on your Cloud CRM before engaging them.  On the customer's browser tab, you may add or read notes entered by your team mates or by you in the Cloud Note section of the customer's profile page.  Cloud Note is a also a way for you and your team mates to make your customers feel special because these notes help you remember and review conversations that may be important to ensuring a successful transaction or just small talk used for building relationships.
            </div> <br />
      </div>

      <div id="Address" style="padding-left:15%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> Address </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify;">
            Clicking or touching a specific company address will result in Google Maps being launched in a new browser tab.  This new browser tab will display the address information of your client in Google Maps.  Results may vary depending on location of your client and the quality of your client's address information.
            </div> <br />
      </div>

      <div id="Estimated-Value" style="padding-left:15%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> Estimated Value </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify;">
            The estimated value field lets you put in an estimate of how much this client can add to your monthly sales performance.  Filling up this field enables you to sort your tables according to value, and thus enable you to plan your customer calls based on biggest sale potential.
            </div> <br />
      </div>

      <div id="Estimated-Close-Date" style="padding-left:15%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> Estimated Close Date </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify;">
            This is your estimate of when the client will place an order with you.  By filling up this field, you can sort your tables and plan your day or week by prioritizing clients who are about to order from you.  This makes for an action-packed day or week that is characterized by a lot of deal closings.
            </div> <br />
      </div>

      <div id="Rating" style="padding-left:15%; padding-right:10%">
            <div style="font-size:x-large; font-weight:bold"> Rating </div> <br />
            <div style="font-size:large; text-align:justify;">
            You can rate your client as being either: <br />
            "Cold", "Warm" or "Hot".  <br /> <br />
            When you rate a client as "Cold" in any of the "My Leads" or "My Qualified Prospects" tab, that client with the cold rating is automatically sent to the "My Leads" tab.  Clients listed on the "My Closed Deals" tab will be transferred to the "My Leads" tab (in case of a Cold Rating) only after 15 days from their last invoice date. <br /> <br />
            When you rate a client as either "Warm" or "Hot" in any of the "My Leads" or "My Qualified Prospects" tab, that client with the "Warm" or "Hot" rating is automatically moved to the "My Qualified Prospects" tab.  Clients listed on the "My Closed Deals" tab will be transferred to the "My Qualified Prospects" tab (in case of a Warm or Hot Rating) only after 15 days from their last invoice date.
            </div> <br />
      </div>

</body>
</html>